 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:13
  |
3 | p.facet(by: [site, region])
  |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ not a variable of d
  |
  = help: the variables of `d` are: site, week, arm, count

== a_variable_named_twice
error[Z0401]: `by:` of `facet` names `site` twice
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:13
  |
3 | p.facet(by: [site, site])
  |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^ one variable, twice
  |
  = help: a plot is parted by each variable once; leave the second out

== a_variable_in_quotation_marks
error[Z0401]: `by` of `facet` must be a Var or Vars, but this is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:13
  |
3 | p.facet(by: "site")
  |             ^^^^^^ a Str
  |
  = help: usage: `p.facet(by: Var | Vars, rows: Var, cols: Var, scales: fixed | free | free_x | free_y = fixed)`

== a_number
error[Z0401]: `by` of `facet` must be a Var or Vars, but this is an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:13
  |
3 | p.facet(by: 3)
  |             ^ an Int
  |
  = help: usage: `p.facet(by: Var | Vars, rows: Var, cols: Var, scales: fixed | free | free_x | free_y = fixed)`

== facets_of_a_frame
error[Z0401]: `facet` cannot be called on a Frame
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:1
  |
3 | d.facet(by: site)
  | ^ this is a Frame
  |
  = help: `facet` takes a Plot first; `x.facet(...)` is `facet(x, ...)`

== a_grid_with_by
error[Z0401]: `by:` of `facet` lays the panels one after another, and `rows:` and `cols:` lay them in a grid: a plot has one or the other
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:25
  |
3 | p.facet(by: site, cols: arm)
  |                         ^^^ a grid, with `by:`
  |
  = help: for a grid write `facet(rows: union, cols: female)`; for a panel for each pair of values, one after another, write `facet(by: [union, female])`

== rows_with_by
error[Z0401]: `by:` of `facet` lays the panels one after another, and `rows:` and `cols:` lay them in a grid: a plot has one or the other
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:32
  |
3 | p.facet(by: [site, arm], rows: week)
  |                                ^^^^ a grid, with `by:`
  |
  = help: for a grid write `facet(rows: union, cols: female)`; for a panel for each pair of values, one after another, write `facet(by: [union, female])`

== one_variable_down_and_across
error[Z0401]: `rows:` and `cols:` of `facet` both name `site`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:3:27
  |
3 | p.facet(rows: site, cols: site)
  |                           ^^^^ the variable of the rows
  |
  = help: a grid has one variable down the page and another across it; for one panel for each value of `site` write `facet(by: site)`

